// pfodWeb NOTE: dedicated-hardware pin-exclusion audit, 2026-07-13.
// Board: Soldered "NULA Max RP2350" (RP2350B - the 48-GPIO variant -
// dual Cortex-M33 @150MHz, 520KB SRAM, 16MB flash, DVI/HDMI output,
// microSD slot, Qwiic/easyC I2C connector, JST Li-Ion battery connector
// with onboard charger, Raspberry Pi Radio Module 2 [RM2, CYW43439-based]
// for WiFi/Bluetooth). Confirmed this repo's "soldered_nula_rp2350"
// variant directory name maps to the "NULA Max RP2350" product - it is
// the ONLY RP2350-based board in Soldered's "NULA Boards" collection
// (the others are NULA Mini ESP32-C6, NULA DeepSleep ESP32-S3, NULA
// Core); no plain, non-"Max" "Nula RP2350" product exists.
//
// No board.json override existed before this audit - the rp2040w chip
// bucket's own board.json documents this board as one of several
// "self-contained vendor files with their own real pin layouts" in this
// bucket, meaning every GPIO with ANY alias in this board's own
// pins_arduino.h (variants/rp2040/rp2040w/soldered_nula_rp2350/
// pins_arduino.h) defaulted to full digital_input/digital_output/
// pwm_output via build_boards.js's buildEsp32Board() - including the
// onboard WiFi radio's power-enable line, the onboard USER button, and
// (via a bare "D33" alias with no bus-role tag at all) the onboard
// microSD card's dedicated chip-select pin. The onboard WS2812 NeoPixel
// LED had NO alias whatsoever (its pins_arduino.h declaration is a bare
// `#define PIN_NEOPIXEL (26u)`, which build_boards.js's alias parser
// does not recognise - only `static const uint8_t` declarations count),
// so it was entirely ABSENT from the generated pin list until this audit
// added it via chipGpios.
//
// Sources consulted:
//  - This board's own pins_arduino.h (variants/rp2040/rp2040w/
//    soldered_nula_rp2350/pins_arduino.h), full file read directly.
//    Key findings: `#include <cyw43_wrappers.h>` (confirms CYW43-family
//    radio); `#define PIN_NEOPIXEL (26u)` / `NUM_NEOPIXEL (1u)` under a
//    "//LEDs" comment (bare #define, no D26 alias - previously invisible
//    to build_boards.js entirely); `static const uint8_t WRL_ON = (23u);`
//    under "// WiFi power GPIO"; `static const uint8_t USER_BTN = (27u);`
//    under "// User button"; a dedicated "// SD Card SPI" bus block
//    (PIN_SPI1_MISO=30/MOSI=31/SCK=32/SS=33) with `#define PIN_SPI1_SS
//    (33u) // CS pin for SD card.` directly on the SS line - distinct
//    from the plain, unlabeled "// SPI0" bus (MISO=2/MOSI=3/SCK=4/SS=5)
//    used for general/header SPI. GPIO30/31 (SPI1 MISO/MOSI) are also
//    aliased as Wire1 SDA1/SCL1 (PIN_WIRE1_SDA=30/SCL=31), i.e. an
//    alternate I2C1 role - this board's own file gives no D30 alias at
//    all (only SDA1), consistent with GPIO30 being header/connector-
//    exposed for a user-selected purpose rather than SD-only. GPIO32
//    (SPI1 SCK) has only a plain D32 alias and no alternate documented
//    role. `static const uint8_t SD_ENABLE = (4u);` under "// SD Card
//    detect - Active Low" and `static const uint8_t
//    PERIPHERAL_POWER_ENABLE = (7u);` under "// Power enable for
//    peripherals - qwiic, sd, rgb. Default HIGH via HW jumper." and
//    `static const uint8_t BATT_ALRT_N = (6u);` under "// Low battery
//    alert - Active Low" - all three share their GPIO with a plain D<n>
//    alias already (D4/D6/D7) and are described as jumper-configurable/
//    board-specific-use signals, not fixed dedicated silicon (see
//    per-pin reasoning below). GPIO12-19/24/25/28/29/36-39 have NO alias
//    of any kind in this file.
//  - Official raspberrypi/pico-sdk board-support header, fetched
//    directly (raw.githubusercontent.com/raspberrypi/pico-sdk/master/
//    src/boards/include/boards/soldered_nula_max_rp2350.h) - this is the
//    authoritative, vendor-contributed board-definition header upstream
//    in the official Pico SDK (title comment: "Board definition for the
//    Soldered NULA Max RP2350"). Confirms, independently of this repo's
//    own pins_arduino.h:
//      `#define SOLDERED_NULA_MAX_RP2350_USER_BTN 27` (matches USER_BTN)
//      `#define PICO_DEFAULT_WS2812_PIN 26` (matches PIN_NEOPIXEL)
//      `#define SOLDERED_NULA_MAX_RP2350_HDMI_CLK_N 12` / `_CLK_P 13` /
//        `_D0_N 14` / `_D0_P 15` / `_D1_N 16` / `_D1_P 17` / `_D2_N 18` /
//        `_D2_P 19` - confirms GPIO12-19 are dedicated DVI/HDMI
//        differential-pair output lines, matching the product's "DVI
//        output" feature. Already fully absent from this board's own
//        pins_arduino.h alias list (no D12-D19 declared anywhere) - i.e.
//        already correctly excluded from the generated pin set by
//        omission; no chipGpios entry added or needed for them.
//      `PICO_DEFAULT_I2C_SDA_PIN 8` / `_SCL_PIN 9` ("Qwiic connector is
//        on these pins") - matches this board's own PIN_WIRE0_SDA=8/
//        SCL=9 exactly.
//      `PICO_DEFAULT_UART_TX_PIN 40` / `_RX_PIN 41`, `PICO_DEFAULT_SPI_*`
//        pins 35-38 - these are the pico-sdk's own "default peripheral"
//        picks (a different numbering convention/instance than this
//        board's Arduino-core PIN_SERIAL1_TX/RX=0/1 and PIN_SPI0_*=2-5),
//        not a conflict - RP2350 GPIOs are function-mux-routable to
//        multiple peripheral instances; not acted on here (out of scope,
//        no button/LED/dedicated-hardware significance).
//      `PICO_SD_CLK_PIN 2` / `PICO_SD_CMD_PIN 0` / `PICO_SD_DAT0_PIN 3` /
//        `PICO_SD_DAT3_PIN 1 // DAT3 of the SD card is the chip select
//        pin` - the pico-sdk's own generic 1-bit-SDIO-mode default pin
//        picks for boards that declare SD support at all; NOTE this
//        does NOT match this board's own pins_arduino.h, which instead
//        gives the microSD card its own dedicated SPI1 bus at GPIO30-33
//        (see above) and leaves GPIO0-3 as plain Serial1 TX/RX (0/1) and
//        general SPI0 MISO/MOSI (2/3). Given this board's own
//        arduino-pico pins_arduino.h is the actual, authoritative source
//        the Designer's generated sketches compile against (not the
//        pico-sdk's bare-metal default-pin scheme, which is a separate,
//        generic fallback not necessarily wired to real silicon on every
//        SD-capable board), GPIO0-3 are NOT treated as SD-dedicated here
//        - no chipGpios override added for them. This SD_CLK/CMD/DAT0/
//        DAT3 pico-sdk default appears to be unused/inapplicable
//        boilerplate for this specific board's Arduino-core integration.
//  - soldered.com product listing (soldered.com/product/nula-max-rp2350/),
//    fetched directly. Confirms: "WS2812 RGB LED" (NeoPixel-style
//    addressable LED - matches GPIO26); "RESET, BOOTSEL, and USER
//    buttons" (three buttons total - RESET is a hardware reset line, not
//    a GPIO; BOOTSEL is the standard RP2040/RP2350-family boot-ROM
//    button, not a normal digitalRead()-capable GPIO on this family,
//    matching this repo's existing convention of never tagging BOOTSEL;
//    USER is the GPIO27 USER_BTN); "Raspberry Pi Radio Module 2
//    providing reliable and native WiFi and Bluetooth connectivity"
//    (confirms the RM2/CYW43439 radio, same module family already
//    researched for sibling board sparkfun_thingplusrp2350); "JST
//    Li-Ion battery connector" with "onboard charger included" (context
//    for BATT_ALRT_N - a charger-IC status signal, not vendor-named
//    beyond this board's own pins_arduino.h comment).
//  - docs.soldered.com/nula-max-rp2350/hardware/ (official hardware-
//    details doc page), fetched directly. Confirms a jumper table:
//    JP1 (default NC) "Disconnects Power LED to reduce standby current"
//    (a fixed power-indicator LED, not a GPIO - no action); JP2 (default
//    NC) "Enables MicroSD chip select line"; JP3 (default NC) "Connects
//    GPIO4 to the MicroSD card power enable line" (directly corroborates
//    this board's own SD_ENABLE=GPIO4 alias, and confirms it is
//    jumper-gated and NOT connected by default); JP4 (default NO) "Keeps
//    the microSD card powered at all times when closed"; JP5 (default
//    NC) "Enables Qwiic I2C interface". The page states the hardware/
//    schematic repository for this board is "not available yet" (still
//    being published by Soldered), so exact per-net schematic labels for
//    JP2's "chip select line" target and the RM2 radio's control-line
//    wiring were not independently re-derivable beyond this jumper table
//    and the pins_arduino.h/pico-sdk sources above.
//  - github.com/raspberrypi/pico-sdk issue #2816 ("Add Soldered NULA Max
//    RP2350 board file") - confirms the board-support header above is a
//    genuine, recently-added (2026) vendor contribution, not a stale or
//    speculative file.
//
// Per-pin findings and decisions:
//
//  GPIO23 (WRL_ON): EXCLUDED, capabilities: []. CONFIRMED WiFi/BT radio
//    (RM2/CYW43439) power-enable control line via this board's own
//    pins_arduino.h comment "// WiFi power GPIO" + the product's
//    confirmed RM2 radio. A sketch that treats this as a plain digital
//    output (e.g. for LED blinking or general I/O) risks powering the
//    radio off mid-session or interfering with the CYW43 driver's own
//    enable-sequencing at startup - same functional hazard already
//    documented for other RM2/CYW43-family radio-control pins in this
//    chip bucket (see rpipicow/rpipico2w's GPIO23/24/25/29 findings and
//    sparkfun_thingplusrp2350's WL_ON research). No SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/
//    MISO/SCK bus-alias collision on GPIO23 (this board's generic SS/
//    MOSI/MISO/SCK/SDA/SCL aliases resolve to GPIO2/3/4/5/8/9), so no
//    pins_arduino.h edit was needed to prevent an unwanted auto-appended
//    bus tag.
//
//  GPIO26 (PIN_NEOPIXEL, no pins_arduino.h D<n> alias at all): ADDED,
//    capabilities: ["digital_output","led_neopixel","pwm_output"].
//    CONFIRMED onboard WS2812 addressable RGB LED via this board's own
//    pins_arduino.h (NUM_NEOPIXEL=1) + the official pico-sdk board
//    header (PICO_DEFAULT_WS2812_PIN 26) + soldered.com's own product
//    listing ("WS2812 RGB LED"). digital_input omitted, matching this
//    repo's established led_neopixel precedent (sparkfun_thingplusrp2350
//    GPIO14, esp32/esp32c61 GPIO8).
//
//  GPIO27 (USER_BTN): RESTRICTED, capabilities: ["digital_input",
//    "button"] (digital_output/pwm_output dropped from the otherwise-
//    default full I/O set). CONFIRMED onboard USER button via this
//    board's own pins_arduino.h ("// User button") + the official
//    pico-sdk board header (SOLDERED_NULA_MAX_RP2350_USER_BTN 27) +
//    soldered.com's own product listing ("RESET, BOOTSEL, and USER
//    buttons"). digital_output/pwm_output deliberately omitted - no
//    source confirms driving this line as output is electrically safe,
//    matching this repo's conservative precedent for board user-buttons
//    (e.g. pimoroni_pico_plus_2w GPIO45).
//
//  GPIO33 (PIN_SPI1_SS, aliased only as plain "D33" - no SS-style alias
//    that build_boards.js's automatic bus-tag matching would recognise,
//    since consts.SS resolves to PIN_SPI0_SS=5 on this board, not
//    PIN_SPI1_SS): EXCLUDED, capabilities: []. CONFIRMED onboard microSD
//    card chip-select via this board's own pins_arduino.h comment
//    ("// SD Card SPI" bus header + "// CS pin for SD card" directly on
//    PIN_SPI1_SS) - same confirmation standard already used for
//    sparkfun_thingplusrp2350's GPIO9 (also commented "CS pin for SD
//    card", also excluded). No legitimate general-purpose or bus-role
//    capability applies - a dedicated SD chip-select is never meant to
//    be user-toggled as plain digital I/O.
//
//  GPIO30/31/32 (PIN_SPI1_MISO/MOSI/SCK - the rest of the "SD Card SPI"
//    bus): NO CHANGE, left at chip-derived general-purpose defaults.
//    GPIO30/31 are also aliased as this board's Wire1 SDA1/SCL1
//    (PIN_WIRE1_SDA/SCL), i.e. an alternate, user-selectable I2C1 role -
//    this indicates the pins are genuinely broken out/shared rather than
//    SD-internal-only, matching this repo's existing policy for
//    dual-purpose SPI buses (sparkfun_thingplusrp2350's SPI0 SCK/MOSI/
//    MISO, left general-purpose because also header-exposed). GPIO32
//    has no alternate alias but no source confirms it is SD-exclusive
//    either (unlike GPIO33's explicit CS comment) - left unchanged,
//    lower-confidence but consistent with the conservative "don't
//    exclude without a direct dedicated-pin confirmation" policy. Only
//    GPIO33's unambiguous "CS pin for SD card" comment met that bar.
//
//  GPIO4 (SD_ENABLE) / GPIO5 (PIN_SPI0_SS) / GPIO6 (BATT_ALRT_N) /
//    GPIO7 (PERIPHERAL_POWER_ENABLE): NO CHANGE, left at chip-derived
//    general-purpose defaults (GPIO5 additionally keeps its automatic
//    "spi_ss" bus tag via the existing SS-alias match). Reasoning:
//      - GPIO4 (SD_ENABLE / "SD Card detect - Active Low"): the official
//        hardware-details page's JP3 entry ("Connects GPIO4 to the
//        MicroSD card power enable line", default NC) confirms this
//        connection is jumper-gated and NOT present by default - this is
//        a board-specific-use, user-configurable signal, not fixed
//        dedicated silicon, matching this repo's existing precedent for
//        jumper/board-specific power-enable pins (sparkfun_thingplusrp2350
//        GPIO13 RT9080 EN - NO CHANGE).
//      - GPIO5 (PIN_SPI0_SS): possibly related to JP2 ("Enables MicroSD
//        chip select line", default NC), also jumper-gated and not
//        connected by default; remains the general-purpose SPI0 SS pin.
//      - GPIO6 (BATT_ALRT_N / "Low battery alert - Active Low"): a
//        likely status/alert signal from the onboard Li-Ion charger IC
//        (product listing confirms "onboard charger included"), but no
//        vendor source specifically documents this pin as unsafe to
//        drive as an output or as permanently hardwired without a
//        jumper - left general-purpose per this audit's "confirm via
//        real documentation, don't guess a restriction" policy.
//      - GPIO7 (PERIPHERAL_POWER_ENABLE / "Power enable for peripherals
//        - qwiic, sd, rgb. Default HIGH via HW jumper."): explicitly
//        described in this board's own pins_arduino.h as jumper-
//        configurable (matches JP5 "Enables Qwiic I2C interface" and/or
//        JP4 "Keeps the microSD card powered at all times when closed"
//        territory) - board-specific-use, not silicon-dedicated, same
//        NO CHANGE precedent as GPIO4 above.
//
//  GPIO12-19 (HDMI/DVI CLK/D0/D1/D2 N/P differential pairs): NO CHANGE
//    NEEDED - already fully absent from this board's own pins_arduino.h
//    alias list (confirmed via direct read - no D12-D19 declared
//    anywhere), so already correctly excluded from the generated pin set
//    by omission. Confirmed as dedicated DVI/HDMI output lines via the
//    official pico-sdk board header's SOLDERED_NULA_MAX_RP2350_HDMI_*
//    defines. No chipGpios entry added (would incorrectly re-introduce
//    pins not meant to be general-purpose I/O).
//
//  GPIO24/25/28/29/36-39 (no alias in pins_arduino.h, no known dedicated
//    function identified in any source consulted): NO CHANGE - already
//    excluded from the generated pin set by omission; no evidence they
//    are anything other than simply unbroken-out/unused GPIOs on this
//    board, so no chipGpios entry was fabricated for them.
//
//  GPIO0/1 (PIN_SERIAL1_TX/RX): NO CHANGE NEEDED - unlike several sibling
//    boards in this chip bucket (sparkfun_thingplusrp2350, rpipico2w),
//    this board's own pins_arduino.h already declares proper bare
//    `TX`/`RX` aliases (`static const uint8_t RX = PIN_SERIAL1_RX;` /
//    `TX = PIN_SERIAL1_TX;`), so build_boards.js's g===tx/g===rx
//    serial-role detection already correctly fires - no pre-existing gap
//    to flag for this board.
//
//  BOOTSEL/RESET: NO CHANGE (no "button" tag) - RESET is a hardware
//    reset line, not a GPIO; BOOTSEL is read via the boot ROM, not a
//    normal digitalRead()-capable GPIO on this family, matching this
//    repo's universal convention of never tagging Pico-family BOOTSEL as
//    a general-purpose "button".
//
// See boardsDetails/rp2040/rp2040w/soldered_nula_rp2350/notes.txt for the
// full research trail.
{
  "boardName": "RP2040W",
  "displayName": "Raspberry Pi Pico W / 2W",
  "family": "rp2040",
  "inputOnlyGpios": [],
  "connections": ["serial", "tcp", "http", "ble"],
  "pinNotes": {},
  "chipGpios": {
    "23": { "capabilities": [], "note": "WiFi/BT radio (Raspberry Pi RM2 / CYW43439) power-enable line (WRL_ON) - dedicated radio control signal, not general purpose. Confirmed via this board's own pins_arduino.h comment \"// WiFi power GPIO\" + official product listing confirming a Raspberry Pi Radio Module 2 (RM2, CYW43439-based) WiFi/Bluetooth radio, matching the same dedicated-enable-line pattern documented for other RM2-equipped boards in this repo (e.g. sparkfun_thingplusrp2350)." },
    "26": { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "led_neopixel", "pwm_output"], "note": "Onboard WS2812 addressable RGB LED (PIN_NEOPIXEL/NUM_NEOPIXEL=1 in this board's own pins_arduino.h; no D26 alias otherwise exists since PIN_NEOPIXEL is a bare #define). Confirmed via the official raspberrypi/pico-sdk board header boards/soldered_nula_max_rp2350.h (PICO_DEFAULT_WS2812_PIN 26) and soldered.com's own product listing (\"WS2812 RGB LED\")." },
    "27": { "capabilities": ["digital_input", "button"], "note": "Onboard USER button (USER_BTN alias in this board's own pins_arduino.h). Confirmed via the official raspberrypi/pico-sdk board header boards/soldered_nula_max_rp2350.h (SOLDERED_NULA_MAX_RP2350_USER_BTN 27) and soldered.com's own product listing (\"RESET, BOOTSEL, and USER buttons\"). digital_output/pwm_output deliberately omitted - no vendor source confirms driving this line as output is safe, matching this repo's conservative precedent for board user-buttons (e.g. pimoroni_pico_plus_2w GPIO45)." },
    "33": { "capabilities": [], "note": "Onboard microSD card chip-select (SPI1 SS). Confirmed via this board's own pins_arduino.h comments (\"// SD Card SPI\" bus header + \"// CS pin for SD card\" directly on PIN_SPI1_SS) - same dedicated-CS confirmation standard already used for sparkfun_thingplusrp2350's GPIO9 (also commented \"CS pin for SD card\", also excluded). This board's generic SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK aliases resolve to SPI0 (GPIO2-5), not SPI1, so GPIO33 carries no automatic bus-role tag - capabilities:[] fully excludes it from general I/O as intended." }
  },
  "pwm": { "min": 0, "max": 255, "method": "analogWrite" },
  "dac": {},
  "adc": { "bits": 12, "max": 4095, "defaultRefVolts": "3.3" }
}
